# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. No journal content may ever be committed.
#
# Primary defense is that journals live OUTSIDE this repo entirely
# (see PLAN.md → "Hard constraint: this repo will be public").
# Everything here is a backstop for mistakes.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT untrack an already-tracked file.
# If something slips in, remove it from history BEFORE pushing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Journal source documents ─────────────────────────────────
data/
journals/
journal-data/
*.doc
*.docx
*.rtf
*.odt
*.pages
*.pdf

# Converted journals land as .txt — blanket-ignore is safer than
# enumerating. Use .md for anything that SHOULD be committed.
*.txt

# ── Derived artifacts that embed journal text verbatim ───────
# The vector index stores original chunk text alongside each
# embedding — it is effectively a copy of the journals.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.lance
.lancedb/
chroma/
.chroma/
index/
embeddings/
*.parquet
*.npy
*.pkl
manifest.csv
eval/
cache/
.cache/
logs/
*.log

# ── Notebooks ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Outputs capture retrieved journal excerpts and are saved INSIDE
# the .ipynb file. .gitignore can't help — the notebook is meant
# to be tracked. Use nbstripout as a git filter to clear outputs.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── The archive's own place names, used by the pre-commit hook ───
private-names.txt

# ── Private working docs (README.md is the tracked one) ──────
PLAN.md

# ── Local config containing the real data path ───────────────
config.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# ── macOS / editors ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.vscode/settings.json
